      "recovery_log": [
        {
          "script": "reopen-implementer-slot.sh",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-27T02:15:26.758Z",
          "task_group": "2.3.a",
          "reason": "Prior implementer claimed T2.3.2 complete but mesh-dev.html does not satisfy the user-visual acceptance criterion: element strokes invisible, magnet poles share one color (4 PMSM poles render as a uniform red ring), no zoom/pan to inspect dense gap layers (~1mm band invisible at default zoom). User-reported on attempting visual ack. Coordinator made two in-place fixes (caller-installed ctx transform + removal of hardcoded lineWidth in MotorMeshView.draw) which got the mesh rendering visible — but the page still cannot support a meaningful visual check."
        },
        {
          "script": "reopen-implementer-slot.sh",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-27T02:47:01.401Z",
          "task_group": "2.3.a",
          "reason": "User-visual ack cannot pass on the existing 15 educational-scale fixtures (audit found pole-4/Q-12/teeth-4-6 monotony, SR 4/4 produces zero torque, hybrid stepper has 5 teeth instead of 50, etc.). User requires industrial-scale realistic fixtures (PMSM 8p/48s, hybrid stepper 50 teeth, SR 8/6, induction 4p/36s/28bars, etc., per coordinator's audit table) plus per-class radii variation. Prior implementer's viz work (visible edges, magnet pole differentiation, zoom/pan, difference-mode stroke) is correct and must be preserved."
        },
        {
          "script": "reopen-implementer-slot.sh",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-27T03:40:38.315Z",
          "task_group": "2.3.a",
          "reason": "Phase 2.5 winding-model cleanup approved by user (2026-05-27). Industrial-scale fixtures from prior round are correct on geometry but sit on the broken cage-as-winding + over-strict validator + p-semantic ambiguity. Spec: spec/phase-2.5-winding-model-cleanup.md. Treat as expanded batch-6 scope; T2.3.2 user-visual ack will only be possible after this lands."
        },
        {
          "script": "reopen-implementer-slot.sh",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-27T06:04:46.002Z",
          "task_group": "2.3.a",
          "reason": "Mesher correctness bugs surfaced by industrial-scale fixtures: (1) lib/motor-mesh.js buildAngularColumns uses 'LCM of rational denominators' for feature alignment, which explodes baseN to ~1300 for fixtures with non-clean feature edges (brushed-dc-pm rotor: 50160 elements vs ~2000 expected). (2) refine knob clamped to [1,inf) so refine<1 has no effect. (3) dofBudget knob does not influence element count. User chose 'fix both properly'."
        },
        {
          "script": "reopen-implementer-slot.sh",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-27T08:09:39.828Z",
          "task_group": "2.3.a",
          "reason": "Phase 2.6 physics-driven mesh sizing approved by user. Spec: spec/phase-2.6-physics-driven-mesh-sizing.md. Treat as continued batch-6 scope; T2.3.2 user-visual ack pending. Prior implementers' work (Phase 2.5 cage routing, mesher correctness fix, LOD viz, fixtures industrial-scale) is correct and must be preserved."
        },
        {
          "script": "reopen-implementer-slot.sh",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-27T09:07:45.642Z",
          "task_group": "2.3.a",
          "reason": "Distributed-winding over-meshing surfaced by user. Specific bug: brushed-dc-pm rotor, brushed-dc-wound rotor, universal rotor all get ~147 cells per slot (1920 angular cells / ~13 features). bldc stator gets 26 cells/slot (1440 / 55). Mesher densities are 18-50x inconsistent across fixtures (7.8 on PMSM stator vs 147 on brushed-DC-PM rotor). Root cause: LCM-cap fallback in buildAngularColumns produces unbounded nBandsPerSector*P_body cell count, ignoring any per-feature target. Need explicit cap at ~8 cells per feature (visualization-grade default), scalable via refine."
        },
        {
          "script": "reopen-implementer-slot.sh",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-27T12:25:52.409Z",
          "task_group": "2.3.b",
          "reason": "Architecture change: prior Phase 2.7 implementation used uniform-Delta-theta + LCM which produced under-mesh on magnet rotors (PMSM 9 cpp) and over-mesh on irrational-angle fixtures (universal 204 cpp). Revised spec (per-feature columns + uniform gap band + constraint matrix) requires from-scratch implementation. Implementation reverted by user."
        }
